# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template: it must be committed so `Copy-Item .env.example
# .env.local` (see SETUP-WINDOWS.md) has something to copy from. It never
# contains a real secret -- only placeholders and generation instructions.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

/app/generated/prisma

# Milestone 16 (Production Readiness) finding: `next dev` (Next.js 16.4.4)
# writes this file at the repo root on its own -- generic AI-agent
# guidance by default, plus a data-sharing "report feedback to Vercel"
# block if `experimental.agentFeedback` is ever turned on (it has been
# turned off; see next.config.ts and docs/production/SECURITY-REVIEW.md
# section 0). Either way it is dev-server scaffolding, not application
# source, and must never be committed.
/AGENTS.md
